# Lead Cat core

- Single-purpose **Google Meet meetings-management Telegram Mini App**. Employees schedule, edit, and cancel meetings inside Telegram; the system creates Google Calendar events and sends notifications via a Telegram bot.
- One Postgres workspace + one Google service-account organizer (no multi-tenancy).
- Deploy: Dokploy with Postgres + Redis + app container — see `docs/DEPLOY-DOKPLOY.md`.
- Auth: TMA JWT primary — see `lead-cat-auth.mdc` and `docs/AUTH.md`.
- Product behavior source of truth: `docs/NEW-FEATURES.md` (ТЗ). Engineering summary: `docs/MEETINGS.md`.
- UI: cat design mandatory — see `cat-design.mdc`.
- KISS / DRY / SOLID; Clean Architecture in Go (`backend/`) — see `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`; lite FSD in `frontend/` — see `frontend-fsd.mdc`.
- Update `docs/*` when changing API, env, auth, or deploy.
